cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Kitchen Rush, please cite it and identify the evaluated protocol."
title: "Kitchen Rush: Useful Work under Resource Budgets in Unfamiliar Kitchens"
abstract: >-
  Kitchen Rush evaluates model action selection in generated kitchen tasks. Models receive
  the same public state and candidate actions, including invalid choices, and complete
  orders under episode-wide resource allowances. The shared dollar view compares task
  quality and actual inference cost; a separate generation-token view measures compatible
  models under enforced token allowances. Recipes and public cooking rules vary across
  instances. Inference pauses kitchen time, so provider response latency does not affect
  scores. V2 results are distinct from the archived v1 latency-based protocol.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Eledath
    given-names: Bassim
repository-code: "https://github.com/bassimeledath/kitchen-rush"
url: "https://github.com/bassimeledath/kitchen-rush"
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - action selection
  - token efficiency
  - inference cost
  - generalization
  - large language models
